%S A399088 1,1,2,1,1,3,1,2,1,1,4,2,2,1,1,3,3,1,1,5,1,1,2,1,1,3,1,1,2,1,4,2,3,3,
%T A399088 1,1,2,1,2,1,1,2,1,1,3,1,2,1,1,4,1,2,1,1,3,2,2,1,1,5,2,1,1,3,1,1,3,1,
%U A399088 1,4,1,1,2,1,3,1,2,7,1,1,2,1,3,1,1,2,1,1,4
%N A399088 The maximum exponent in the prime factorization of the number following the n-th squarefree number.
%C A399088 Let d(k) = zeta(2) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^2 - 1/p^k). Then, the asymptotic density of the occurrences of 1 in this sequence is d(2) = 0.53071182... (A065469), and the asymptotic density of the occurrences of k >= 2 is d(k+1) - d(k).
%H A399088 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A399088/b399088.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A399088 a(n) = A051903(A005117(n)+1).
%F A399088 a(A071403(n)) = A023510(n).
%F A399088 Asymptotic mean: Limit_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} a(k) = 1 + Sum_{k>=2} (1-d(k)) = 1.86972420871420434795..., where d(k) is defined in the Comments section.
%t A399088 emax[n_] := Max[FactorInteger[n][[;; , 2]]]; emax /@ (Select[Range[150], SquareFreeQ] + 1)
%o A399088 (PARI) list(kmax) = apply(x -> vecmax(factor(x+1)[,2]), select(issquarefree, [1..kmax]));
%o A399088 (Python)
%o A399088 # uses Python code from A005117
%o A399088 from sympy import factorint
%o A399088 def A399088(n): return max(factorint(A005117(n)+1).values()) # _Chai Wah Wu_, Aug 20 2026
%Y A399088 Cf. A005117, A013661, A023510, A051903, A065469, A071403, A399089.
